  "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID> done. The page is counted the way your note says. https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/18YbQKE2MaVMYQ1NQtuWFDTQHrsyBW0MQ4K_d0UH96BE/edit (shared with you and Blake)\n\n**What each bet cost to build:**\n• Domino Delights: $955,849.64\n• ZM: $544,433.44\n• Combo Fighter: $72,685.61\n\n**What each brought in** (lifetime, warehouse daily revenue table, as recorded):\n• Domino Delights: $12,331.25\n• ZM: $11.99\n\n**What changes on the draft deck:**\n• Build cost: Domino Delights $985K → **$956K**, ZM $609K → **$544K**, Combo Fighter $74K → **$73K**\n• \"What each brought in: to fill in\" → **Domino Delights $12.3K, ZM $12** (nothing for Combo Fighter)\n\n**Why it moved from your quick pass:**\n• Taken out of build: marketing ($16.4K Node Media on DD; $56.5K Adjoe/AppLovin/PlayableX/Brooks on ZM; $1K Brooks on CF) and company spend ($49.6K: Singular, TYZ, trademarks, website, 4X help, plus Martin's laptop at 1,999 BGN, which isn't converted)\n• The $4K to JPMorgan in Aug 2024 was our own Chase account (Blake's email), so it's $0\n• Oleg's $125 wire came back. There's no Payoneer receipt in my mail, so it's $0\n• Leapblock closed their file and reported $407,944 over 30 wires. That's +$33,290 versus the notices, from the Sep 13, 2023 wire, which went to DD. Their number is used and the reason is on ENG-2439\n\nEvery payee has its line, and all 22 issues in Payee history are moved to Done."
 }
